Parfait — on va te préparer comme un Tech Lead premium qui rassure un recruteur RH + donne envie au client 🔥
Objectif : pro, structuré, impactant, sans blabla inutile


---

🎤 1. Ta présentation (pitch 1–2 min)

👉 À dire presque mot pour mot :

> Hello, thanks for having me.

I’m a Senior Java / Angular Engineer with around 10+ years of experience, mainly in banking, financial systems, and secure enterprise environments.

I’ve been working on large-scale applications using Java, Spring Boot, Angular, REST APIs, and relational databases like PostgreSQL.

In my recent roles, especially at Société Générale and IDEMIA, I’ve been acting as a Tech Lead — not just coding, but also guiding architecture, reviewing code, mentoring developers, and ensuring high quality delivery.

I’ve worked in multicultural and international environments, collaborating with teams across different countries, which helped me develop strong communication and coordination skills.

What I enjoy most is building clean, scalable systems and helping teams deliver efficiently while maintaining high engineering standards.

That’s why this Tech Lead role really caught my attention.




---

💼 2. Montrer ton intérêt (important côté RH)

👉 Phrase simple mais stratégique :

> I’m particularly interested in this opportunity because it combines technical leadership, structured environments, and large-scale systems, which is exactly where I bring the most value.



👉 Et tu ajoutes :

> Also, working in a European Commission context is very appealing to me, especially for the impact and the international dimension.




---

🌍 3. Multinational / international (à placer naturellement)

👉 À glisser dans tes réponses :

> I’ve worked with international teams across France, Morocco, and India, which required strong communication, adaptability, and clear coordination.



👉 Option plus forte :

> I’m very comfortable working in multicultural environments and aligning teams with different backgrounds and expectations.




---

🧠 4. Questions RH classiques + réponses solides


---

❓ “Tell me about your Tech Lead experience”

👉 Réponse :

> In my recent roles, I’ve been acting as a Tech Lead on a daily basis.

I was responsible for:

guiding technical decisions and architecture

reviewing code and ensuring best practices

mentoring developers

coordinating with business and other teams


I also helped improve code quality using tools like Sonar, and contributed to CI/CD and testing strategies.




---

❓ “What is your leadership style?”

👉 Réponse (très important) :

> I would describe my leadership style as supportive and pragmatic.

I like to guide the team without micromanaging, help developers grow, and make sure we deliver efficiently.

I focus a lot on clarity, communication, and removing blockers.




---

❓ “How do you handle pressure or deadlines?”

👉 Réponse :

> I prioritize, communicate early, and focus on delivering value incrementally.

I also try to anticipate risks and address them early to avoid last-minute issues.




---

❓ “Why are you looking for a new opportunity?”

👉 Réponse clean :

> I’m looking for a role where I can have more impact as a Tech Lead, contribute to architecture decisions, and work on large-scale systems in an international environment.




---

💰 5. Question TJM / salaire (CRUCIAL)

❓ “What is your daily rate?”

👉 Réponse intelligente (ne te grille pas trop tôt) :

> I’m flexible depending on the scope, responsibilities, and onsite expectations.

For a Tech Lead role in Belgium, I’m generally targeting a range around 650 to 750 euros per day.



👉 Si tu veux jouer plus stratégique :

> I would prefer to better understand the expectations and working conditions before confirming a precise rate.




---

❓ “Are you open to onsite work in Brussels?”

👉 Réponse :

> Yes, I’m open to a near-site setup, as long as it’s balanced. I’m flexible depending on the organization.




---

🔥 6. Tes questions à poser (ultra important)

👉 Tu DOIS poser des questions sinon tu perds des points

Questions intelligentes :

How is the team structured?

What is the level of technical ownership for the Tech Lead?

Are there existing architecture challenges?

What are the main priorities for the next 3–6 months?

What is the onsite / remote balance?


👉 Question qui te positionne senior :

> What are the main technical challenges you expect the Tech Lead to solve?




---

⚡ 7. Ton positionnement final

Tu dois renvoyer cette image :

✅ Pas juste dev
✅ Pas juste lead
👉 Tech Lead qui sécurise delivery + qualité + équipe


---

🚀 Bonus : punchline de fin

> I believe my experience in complex systems and my hands-on leadership approach would allow me to quickly bring value to the team.




---

Si tu veux, je peux te faire : 👉 un pitch ultra premium 30 secondes (version impact max)
👉 ou les réponses techniques probables côté client EU Commission (là ça va être plus costaud 👀)
